!! Run Jasmine tests

The plugin ships with its own minimal test edition:

```
TIDDLYWIKI_CLI_MODE=1 \
  TIDDLYWIKI_PLUGIN_PATH=dev-wiki/plugins \
  npx tiddlywiki dev-wiki/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/test-edition \
  --test --spec="knowledge-app:"
```

Tests live in `test/test-*.js` (tagged `$:/tags/test-spec`):

* `test-helpers.js` — filter `\function`s in the dev-wiki context
* `test-broken-refs.js` — `knowledge-has-broken-ref` filter operator
* `test-pseudo-index.js` — `_index` pseudo (registration + end-to-end resolution)
* `test-areas.js` — area-tiddler shape + ID derivation
* `test-types.js` — type registry shape
* `test-source-helpers.js` — `knowledge.yt-id`, `knowledge.medium-icon`, `knowledge.consume-icon`
* `test-capture-action.js` — the quick-capture action sequence

!! Run Playwright E2E

```
npx playwright test tw-tests/tests/e2e/knowledge-app.spec.js \
  --config tw-tests/playwright.config.js
```

The Playwright wiki (`tw-tests/pw-edition/`) loads the plugin and exposes the HTTP API for fixtures. Note: the existing spec was written against the pre-0.1.20 section-based UI and needs rewriting to match the mindmap-driven shell.

!! Restart rules

| Change | Restart? |
|JS pseudo (`pseudo/_index.js`) | yes (module reload) |
|JS filter (`filters/broken-refs.js`, `filters/active-node-filter.js`) | yes (module reload) |
|JS startup (`modules/focus-rewind.js`) | yes |
|All `.tid` (apps, views, procedures, filters, config, templates) | no (live re-read) |

!! Adding a new note type

# Append an entry to `config/types.tid` (JSON: `id`, `caption`, `icon`, `group`).
# Optional: ship `forms/capture-<id>.tid` (extra modal fields). State tiddlers should live under `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/<id>/<field>`.
# Optional: ship `forms/<id>-helpers.tid` with shared `\function`s; `\import` from the capture form. (`forms/render-<id>` is on hold pending a custom `mm.preview-body-template` that dispatches on `kn.type`.)
# Patch-bump `plugin.info` version + add a `changelog.tid` row.

The new type appears in the quick-capture modal's type select, in the interactive type pill at the top of the mindmap preview, and as a chip in the filter strip above the mindmap.

!! Adding a new mindmap producer arg

`knowledge-tree` lives in `rimir/mindmap` (`producers/knowledge-tree.js`). Add the arg to `exports.describe()`, handle it in `produce()` (or in `applyPostBuildArgs()` for purely post-processing args), and — if reproduce should fire when the arg's referenced tiddlers change — append them via `exports.refreshFilter()`. Update `views/knowledge-mindmap-view.tid`'s `mm.args` JSON to set the new arg.

!! Adding a new area

Create a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/area` with fields `area-id` (the slug), `caption`, `icon`, optional `color`. The topbar's `+ Area` button does this via the area modal. The new area appears as a top-level node in the mindmap and as a pill in the topbar.

